{"name":"Hyper Light Drifter","hex":"#eddbda","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hyper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of hyperextension.","Clipping of hypersexuality."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To subject (a film or plate) to photographic hypersensitization, chiefly as a technique in astrophotography.","To expose (an animal) to a disease-causing organism, to promote hyperimmunity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hyper"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"drifter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who moves from place to place or job to job.","A type of lightweight sail used in light winds like a spinnaker."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who takes part in drift fishing.","A boat used for drift fishing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drifter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hyper Light Drifter","blocks":[{"text":"Hyper Light Drifter is an action role-playing game developed and published by Heart Machine. The Microsoft Windows, Linux and OS X versions were released in March 2016, and the PlayStation 4 and Xbox One versions in July 2016. A Special Edition port of the game, featuring additional content, was released by Abylight Studios for the Nintendo Switch in September 2018, for iOS devices in July 2019 and for Android devices in June 2024."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/HyperLightDrifterBoxArt.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyper_Light_Drifter","wikidata":"Q16457556"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/Hyper_Light_Drifter_Screenshot.png/330px-Hyper_Light_Drifter_Screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/Hyper_Light_Drifter_Screenshot.png/330px-Hyper_Light_Drifter_Screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"When conversing with the inhabitants of the world, the player sees images in place of dialogue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHyper_Light_Drifter_Screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Heart_machine_gdc_2017.jpg/500px-Heart_machine_gdc_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Heart_machine_gdc_2017.jpg/1280px-Heart_machine_gdc_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Heart_machine_gdc_2017.jpg/500px-Heart_machine_gdc_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Heart Machine tea